cision is durably recorded (ADR/AGENTS.md) nor whether thresholds are config-driven vs hardcoded"],"finding":"The fuse thresholds (3 consecutive eligible outcomes, >=2 tickets, >=2 distinct endpoints) and the RetryBudget caps (MAX_INVOCATIONS, MAX_CUMULATIVE_SLEEP_MS) are presented as fixed constants in a new pipeline stage, but the plan does not state whether these evolve-prone thresholds are configurable or captured in an ADR/design-doc beyond this plan text.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5403569368131a9b","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics; Plan step 3","norm_id":"n1324795f20ccd73b","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future operator wants to tune the fuse sensitivity (e.g. 5 consecutive across 3 tickets) and finds the value hardcoded with no documented rationale for the original choice"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the circuit-breaker prior art (e.g. Nygard / Azure / resilience4j) the scoped fuse instantiates and justify its deliberate divergences — no Half-Open probe state and per-pass in-memory (non-durable) counters vs the conventional durable rolling-window breaker — as intentional fits to per-pass reconciliation semantics.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Add a new endpoint-failure scoped fuse (none exists today).'","Plan: 'Per-pass, in-memory, per-scope; zeroed each reconcile_once(pass_id) pass (no durable cross-pass state).'","Retrieved prior art (Azure Architecture Center, resilience4j, microservices.io) documents consecutive-failure-threshold circuit breakers with Closed/Open/Half-Open states as the standard resilience pattern.","The plan justifies novelty only against the repo-internal blast-radius guard, not against the external circuit-breaker lineage its design clearly instantiates."],"finding":"The scoped finite-pass fuse is a variant of the well-established circuit-breaker pattern, but the plan does not name that external prior art or justify its deliberate divergences from the canonical breaker (no Half-Open probe state; per-pass in-memory counters zeroed each reconcile_once instead of a durable rolling-window/interval breaker).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f341a6fb154c951","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 and 'Fuse scope, eligibility & counter semantics' section","norm_id":"n755c8b454a7d26c3","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer needs to know why the fuse lacks a Half-Open probe and durable window that established breakers provide, before committing to the per-pass design.","A future maintainer considers adopting resilience4j-style semantics not realizing the divergences were intentional."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capab